#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
ActiGrid FINAL Reviewer-Clearance Audit
======================================

Purpose
-------
This is a targeted final audit, NOT a rerun of the old 12-hour pipeline.

It addresses the remaining concrete reviewer concerns:
1) DQN/backbone train-row coupling:
   - audit train-vs-validation posterior entropy/confidence on every non-empty mask;
   - run a backbone-training / policy-training holdout DQN control; use group-disjoint groups when class-complete separation is feasible, otherwise a clearly labeled stratified row-disjoint fallback.
2) MSU/ORNL preprocessing hygiene:
   - audit NaN/Inf and exact duplicates across source files/splits;
   - rebuild MSU with train-only median imputation;
   - compare old pooled-imputation HGB vs train-only-imputation HGB;
   - run a stratified random-row HGB sanity split and 5x5 confusion matrix.
3) Low-cost classifier bottleneck:
   - compare neural single-modality performance with per-subset HGB.
4) Fragility interpretation:
   - on the clean disjoint-policy seed-42 control, apply zero, Gaussian N(0,2^2),
     and normal-class mimicry corruption to each modality and compare DQN,
     same-backbone entropy stopping, and full fusion.
5) Paper-ready outputs:
   - compact CSVs, confusion matrices, and FINAL_REVIEWER_CLEARANCE.md.

It deliberately does NOT:
- rerun the 10-seed original controlled study;
- rerun sequential-over-HGB (already completed separately);
- claim equivalence from non-significant tests;
- convert normalized proxy cost into real latency/bandwidth/energy.

Expected Kaggle inputs
----------------------
/kaggle/input/datasets/sazidul001x94/power-system-attack-dataset
/kaggle/input/datasets/sazidul001x94/tu-delft-cyber-physical-power-system-cpps
/kaggle/input/datasets/rejaulislam12/rev-hard

Output
------
/kaggle/working/actigrid/final_reviewer_clearance/
/kaggle/working/actigrid/final_reviewer_clearance.zip
"""

